REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON

ORDER G0 0 0 0 0 16 /MINFI OF

REPUBLIQUE DU CAMEROUN

13 ADUT 2026 ON THE

CLASSIFICATION BY CATEGORY OF PUBLIC ESTABLISHMENTS IN CAMEROON

THE MINISTER OF FINANCE,

MINFUL OF the constitution;

MINFUL OF Law No. 2017/010 of 12 July 2017 on the General Statute of Establishments
Public;

MINFUL OF Law No. 2018/011 of 11 July 2018 on the Code of Transparency and Good

Governance in the Management of Public Finances in Cameroon;

MINFUL OF Decree No. 2011/408 of 11 December 2011 on the organization of the Government,

amended and supplemented by Decree No. 2018/190 of 2 March 2018;

MINFUL OF Decree No. 2018/191 of 2 March 2018 on the reorganization of the Government;

MINFUL OF Decree No. 2019/320 of 19 July 2019 to specify the terms of application of

certain provisions of Laws No. 2017/010 and No. 2017/011 of 12 July 2017 on the general status

of Public Establishments and Public Enterprises;

MINFUL OF Decree No. 2019/322 of 19 June 2019 to set the categories of Public Establishments,

the remuneration, allowances and benefits of their managers,

HEREBYORDERS AS FOLLOWS:

ARTICLE 1.- (1) This Order classifies by category Public Establishments in Cameroon for the
performance achieved for the 2022, 2023 and 2024 fiscal years.

(2) The Public Establishments referred to in paragraph 1 above concern:

traditional public establishments, regardless of the form chosen, whose management is
subject to the fiscal regime of the State;

public establishments of a special nature, operating in the form of a public enterprise, in
particular with regard to accounting and financial management.

ARTICLE 2.- Pursuant to the provisions of Article 11 of Decree No. 2019/322 of 19 June 2019
establishing the categories of Public Establishments, the remuneration, allowances and benefits
of their managers, Public Establishments are classified as follows:

First-class establishments
National Social Insurance Fund (NSIF);
Special Council Fund for mutual Intervention (FEICOM).

Second-category establishments
Telecommunications Regulatory Agency (ART);
Hydrocarbon Price Stabilization Fund (HPSF);
Road Fund (RF).

Third-category establishmen

Cameroon Rural Electrification Agency (AER);

Cameroon Civil Aviation Authority (CCAA);

Cameroon Radio Television (CRTV);

Cocoa and Coffee Value Chain Development Fund (FODECC);
National Employment Fund (NEF);

Douala General Hospital (DGH);

Office du Baccalauréat du Cameroun (OBC).

d) Fourth category establishments

Investment Promotion Agency (API);

Public Procurement Regulatory Agency (ARMP);

Agency for Standards and Quality (ANOR);

National Agency for Technologies, Information and Communication (ANTIC);
Electricity Sector Regulatory Agency (ARSEL);

Autonomous Sinking Fund (CAA);

Centre Pasteur of Cameroon (CPC);

National School of Administration and Magistracy (ENAM);
General Certificate of Education Board (GCE BOARD);
Yaoundé General Hospital (YGH);

Institute of Agricultural Research for Development (IRAD);
National Institute of Statistics (NIS).

Fifth category establishments

National Football Academy (ANAFOOT);

Agency for the Promotion of Small and Medium-Sized Enterprises (APME);
Economic Zone Promotion Agency (APZE);

National Civic Service Agency for Participation in Development (ASCNPD);
Radiological Safety and Nuclear Security Authority (ASRAN);

National Port Authority (NPA);

Central Bureau of Population Censuses (BUCREP);

Cameroon National Civil Registry Office (BUNEC);

Maritime Fisheries Development Fund (CDPM);

North Livestock Development Fund (CDEN);

National Central Supply of Essential Medical Medicines and Consumables
(CENAME);

Maroua Centre for the Rehabilitation of Disabled People (Maroua-NCRDP);
Hospital Centre for Research and Application in Endoscopic Surgery and Human
Reproduction (CHRACERH);

Yaoundé University Teaching Hospital (UTH);

Chantal Biya International Reference Centre (CBIRC);

National Centre for the Rehabilitation of Disabled Persons (NCRDP).

National Blood Transfusion Centre (NBTC);

National Centre for the Study and Experimentation of Agricultural Machinery
(CENEEMA);

Interregional Committee for the Fight against Drought in the North (CILSN);
International School of Security Forces (EIFORCES);

National Advance School of Posts, Telecommunications and Information and
Communication Technologies (SUP'TIC);

National Advance School of Public Works (ENSTP);

Garoua General Hospital (GGH);

Douala Gynaecological, Obstetric and Paediatric Hospital (HGOPED);

Yaoundé Gynaecological-Obstetric and Paediatric Hospital (HGOPY);

National Printing Press (NPP);

Institute of Geological and Mining Research (IRGM);

Institute of Medical Research and Studies of Medicinal Plants (IMPM);

National Institute of Cartography (NIC);

National Institute of Youth and Sports (NIYS);

Higher Institute of Public Management (ISMP);

National Laboratory for Quality Control of Medicines and Expertise
(LANACOME);

Limbe Nautical Arts and Fisheries Institute (LINAFI);

North-West Development Authority (MIDENO);

South-West Development Authority (SOWEDA);

Mission for the Integrated Development of the Mandara Mountains (MIDIMA);
Mission for the Promotion of Local Materials (MIPROMALO);

Mission for the Regulation of the Supply of Consumer Products (MIRAP);

Ocean Development Studies Authority (MEAO);

North Region Development Studies Authority (MEADEN);

National School of Local Administration (NASLA);

Northwest Livestock Development Fund (CDENO);

National Observatory on Climate Change (ONACC);

Cereal Board (OC); ‘

National Cocoa and Coffee Board (ONCC);

National Bureau for Veterans, Former Soldiers and War Victims of Cameroon
(ONACAM);

National Office of Sports Infrastructures and Equipment (ONIES);

Conference Centre (CC);

Cocoa Development Company (SODECAO);

Aerial Agricultural Treatment Unit (UTAVA);

Upper Noun Valley Development Authority (UNVDA).

ARTICLE 3.- The Deposits and Consignments Fund, a public establishment operating in the
financial sector, is governed, with regard to the remuneration scheme for directors and corporate
officers, by the provisions applicable to the banking sector, in accordance with the relevant
Community regulations.

ARTICLE 4.- This Order, which takes effect from the l'* on January 2026, will be updated after
three (03) years, in accordance with the regulations in force.

ARTICLE 5.- This Order shall be registered, published in accordance with the emergency
procedure, and then inserted in the Official Gazette in English and French.

SERVICES DU PREMIER MINISTRE
VISA

THE MINISTER
PRIME MINISTER'S OFFICE

Louis Paul MOTAZE

